  "body": {
    "id": "prop:causal-optimal-value-corollary",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For every \\(P\\in\\mathcal P_{d,\\epsilon}\\), consistency and armwise conditional exchangeability imply\n\\[\n V^\\star(P)=\\Psi\\{\\operatorname{Obs}(P)\\}\n =\\sum_{x=1}^d p_x\\max_{a\\in\\{0,1\\}}\\mu_{ax}.\n\\]\nThus the observed-law target is the unrestricted optimal-treatment value for every causal completion in \\(\\mathcal P_{d,\\epsilon}\\), while the minimax theorems themselves require only the observed law to lie in \\(\\mathcal D_{d,\\epsilon}^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal P_{d,\\epsilon}\\)",
      "\\(d\\)",
      "\\(\\epsilon\\)",
      "\\(V^\\star(P)\\)",
      "\\(\\Psi(\\mathbb P)\\)",
      "\\(\\operatorname{Obs}(P)\\)",
      "\\(x\\)",
      "\\(p_x\\)",
      "\\(a\\)",
      "\\(\\mu_{ax}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal D_{d,\\epsilon}^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:consistency",
      "ass:conditional-exchangeability",
      "def:model-class",
      "def:observed-margin",
      "def:observed-model-class",
      "def:observed-optimal-value",
      "def:oracle-value",
      "prop:identification-and-extension"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(P\\in\\mathcal P_{d,\\epsilon}\\) and put \\(\\mathbb P=\\operatorname{Obs}(P)\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{def:model-class}\\), \\(\\mathbb P\\in\\mathcal D_{d,\\epsilon}^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\).  For an occupied cell \\(x\\), its overlap probabilities are positive, and \\(\\mathrm{ass:conditional-exchangeability}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{ass:consistency}\\) give, separately for each \\(a\\in\\{0,1\\}\\),\n\\[\n E_P\\{Y(a)\\mid X=x\\}\n =E_P\\{Y(a)\\mid A=a,X=x\\}\n =E_P(Y\\mid A=a,X=x)=\\mu_{ax}.                                     \\tag{6}\n\\]\nThe first equality in (6) is armwise conditional independence; the second is consistency on \\(\\{A=a\\}\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{def:oracle-value}\\), finite-support conditioning and (6) imply\n\\[\n V^\\star(P)=\\sum_{x:p_x>0}p_x\\max_a\\mu_{ax}.\n\\]\nNull-cell summands vanish, so \\(\\mathrm{def:observed-optimal-value}\\) identifies the last display with \\(\\Psi(\\mathbb P)\\).  This proves the causal equality rather than placing it in either definition.",
    "justification": "This corollary keeps the causal estimand distinct from the observed-law functional and proves their equality under the stated causal assumptions.",
    "gap": "ZengBalakrishnanHanKennedy2024Discrete explicitly separates its observed regression functional from its causal interpretation; this proposition supplies the corresponding completion and equality for the optimal-regression maximum.",
    "consumer": "Causal applications may invoke the minimax frontier only after checking consistency and armwise exchangeability.",
